

STYLEME 
“Your style, instantly.” 
1. Concept Name 
STYLEME — “Your style, instantly.” 
STYLEME is an in-store augmented reality shopping experience designed to help customers 
discover, virtually try on, and order products that may be unavailable in their size, color or not 
carried in the physical store. 
2. Problem Statement 
Customers may find something they want to purchase in-store, only to discover that the item is 
out of stock, unavailable in their size, or exclusively sold online. This can create a frustrating 
and disappointing shopping experience, especially when customers are already interested in 
making a purchase. 
STYLEME addresses this issue by combining augmented reality, virtual try-on technology, 
trained sales representatives, and handheld devices that allow associates to order products 
directly for customers. Customers can choose to have their purchases shipped to their home or 
sent to the store for pickup. 
To make customers more comfortable with ordering products they cannot physically try on, the 
AR experience allows them to see how selected clothing items could look on their body before 
purchasing. 
Creating a more convenient, comfortable, and reliable shopping experience is important for the 
brand because a frustrating experience can lead to lost sales, decreased customer satisfaction, 
and reduced brand loyalty. 
3. Proposed Digital Experience 
The STYLEME experience would be located inside the store and designed to resemble a 
traditional dressing room so the technology still feels casual, familiar, and comfortable. 
The centerpiece would be an augmented reality mirror that creates a 3D scan of the customer 
and digitally displays selected clothing items on their body. The items would be selected by the 

customer with assistance from a sales representative using a handheld work device that is 
connected to the STYLEME mirror. 
4. How It Works 
1. Select 
 The customer works with a sales representative to select clothing items they are interested in 
trying. 
2. Scan & Try On 
 The customer enters the STYLEME fitting area, where the AR mirror creates a 3D scan and 
virtually displays the selected clothing items on them. 
3. Yes or No 
 While viewing each item, the customer can select ✓ Yes if they like the item or ✕ No if they do 
not. 
4. Notify the Sales Representative 
 Once the customer finishes trying on their selections, they can tap the notification option on the 
mirror. This sends a ping to the sales representative’s work device. 
For privacy and comfort, the sales representative cannot see what is happening inside the fitting 
area while the customer is using the mirror. 
5. Consult & Order 
 After completing the virtual try-on, the customer can meet with the sales representative to 
discuss the items they liked, available sizes, colors, and ordering options. 
6. Choose Delivery 
 The sales representative can place the order using their handheld device. The customer can 
choose to have the item shipped directly to their home or sent to the store for pickup. 
5. Value to the Customer 
STYLEME creates a more convenient, personalized, and inclusive shopping experience. 
● Convenience: Customers can order products that are unavailable in-store without 
having to leave and search for them online themselves. 
● Personalization: Customers can virtually see how different clothing items may look on 
them before deciding what they want to purchase. 
● Inclusivity: The experience can help support customers across a wider range of body 
sizes by making products available beyond the sizes typically stocked in-store. 
● Engagement: Customers interact directly with the technology instead of simply being 
told that an item is unavailable. 

● Empowerment: Customers have more control over what they want to try, what they like 
or dislike, and how they receive their purchase. 
● Comfort: Customers can use the AR mirror privately without the sales representative 
watching their fitting-room experience. 
Overall, STYLEME helps turn an otherwise disappointing “we don’t have your size” 
experience into an opportunity to find and purchase something the customer actually wants. 
6. Value to the Business 
STYLEME could help the business turn missed opportunities into sales by giving customers a 
way to purchase products that are unavailable in their local store. 
Potential business benefits include: 
● Increased sales: Customers can purchase items that are out of stock, unavailable in 
their size, or sold exclusively online. 
● Higher customer satisfaction: Customers receive a solution instead of simply being 
told an item is unavailable. 
● Improved brand perception: Providing an inclusive and technology-driven experience 
can position the brand as more innovative and customer-focused. 
● Greater customer loyalty: A convenient shopping experience can encourage 
customers to return to the brand. 
● More efficient sales support: Sales representatives can use handheld devices to 
quickly locate and order products for customers. 
● Better customer insights: The customer’s Yes/No selections could potentially provide 
the business with insight into customer preferences and product demand. 
7. Key Features 
STYLEME AR Mirror 
An augmented reality mirror that creates a 3D scan of the customer and digitally displays 
selected clothing items for a virtual try-on experience. 
Connected Sales Representative Handheld Device 
A handheld work device used by sales representatives to select products, check availability, and 
assist customers with ordering items. 
Yes / No Selection System 

Customers can select ✓ Yes or ✕ No while virtually trying on each item, allowing them to 
quickly narrow down their choices. 
Sales Representative Notification 
Once customers finish their virtual try-on, they can notify a sales representative directly through 
the mirror. 
Flexible Ordering 
Customers can order their selected items and choose between home delivery or in-store 
pickup. 
Private Experience 
The sales representative receives the customer’s notification but does not have access to view 
the customer inside the fitting area. 
8. Potential Challenges 
Technology Hesitation 
 Some customers may be uncomfortable using new technology or may prefer a traditional 
fitting-room experience. 
Privacy & AI Concerns 
 Customers may worry about the AR system creating a 3D scan of their face or body and how 
that information is stored or used. Clear privacy policies, consent, and data protection would be 
important. 
Accuracy of Virtual Try-On 
 Customers may question whether the clothing will fit or look the same in person as it does 
through augmented reality. The technology would need to provide realistic sizing and fit 
information while making it clear that the virtual experience is an estimate. 
Cost & Maintenance 
 Implementing AR mirrors, 3D scanning technology, connected handheld devices, software, and 
ongoing maintenance could require a significant investment. 
Technology Reliability 
 The experience would depend on reliable software, internet connectivity, and properly 
functioning devices. Technical issues could negatively impact the customer’s experience if not 
addressed quickly. 
 